u-boot: put mainline's console on the rate this board can be typed at

The base device tree - dts/upstream/src/arm64/rockchip/rk3399-orangepi.dts,
shared with Linux - says

    stdout-path = "serial2:1500000n8";

and U-Boot proper honours the rate in stdout-path, so it overrides
CONFIG_BAUDRATE the moment it takes over from SPL. That is the rate this
board's three-pin header cannot take a burst at - see patches/uboot/0001 for
the measurements - which makes the prompt awkward in exactly the situation
you need it.

It was briefly suspected of being why mainline looked like it hung, on the
theory that BL31 and U-Boot proper had moved to 1500000 while the capture
stayed at 115200. That was wrong - the stall was real, and it was SPL loading
a BL31 that overlapped its own text; see "Mainline U-Boot" in
docs/roadmap.md. This patch is what makes the console legible once that is
fixed, not the fix itself.

The value in the kernel's copy of this file is right for the kernel's own
console, so this belongs here rather than in the shared DTS.

diff --git a/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-orangepi-u-boot.dtsi b/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-orangepi-u-boot.dtsi
index b7452eca..86fdba37 100644
--- a/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-orangepi-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/rk3399-orangepi-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -21,3 +21,9 @@
 &vdd_log {
 	regulator-init-microvolt = <950000>;
 };
+
+/ {
+	chosen {
+		stdout-path = "serial2:115200n8";
+	};
+};
